# API documentation (Swagger)

Every backend module, controller, and endpoint must keep Swagger documentation complete. The canonical guide is `docs/backend/API_DOCUMENTATION_GUIDE.md`; read it before creating or modifying controllers and response DTOs.

## Required Workflow

- Order the handlers in every controller by HTTP method: `@Get`/`@Sse` first, then `@Post`, `@Put`, `@Patch`, and `@Delete` last. Never mix the groups.
- Inside each group, declare static routes (`/categories`, `/sales-catalog`) before dynamic ones (`/:id`).
- Add `@ApiTags('<Area>')` at the controller level.
- Add `@ApiOperation({ summary: '<short summary>' })` to every handler.
- Add a success response on every handler:
  - `@ApiResponse({ status, description, type })` with a response DTO class, or
  - `@ApiPaginatedResponse(Model, 'description')` for paginated collections.
- Add the relevant business errors the service actually throws: `400`, `401`, `403`, `404`, `409`.
- Make the documented `status` match the handler's `@HttpCode`.
- Add `@ApiResponse` with `description` (and a type when a DTO exists) for SSE endpoints.
- For webhooks, document the acceptance status and the token/validation errors; use `@ApiExcludeEndpoint()` only with an explicit reason.
- Verify Swagger still builds:

```bash
pnpm --filter backend build
pnpm --filter backend test --runInBand
pnpm --filter backend exec eslint "src/<module>/**/*.ts"
```

## Do Not Do This

- Do not add a controller, route, or module with endpoints that lack `@ApiOperation` and a success `@ApiResponse`.
- Do not document a success response without a `description`.
- Do not use a bare array type for paginated endpoints; use `@ApiPaginatedResponse`.
- Do not invent error codes the service does not throw.
- Do not duplicate `@ApiResponse` for status 200 on top of `@ApiPaginatedResponse`.

## Notes

- `ApiPaginatedResponse` lives in `apps/backend/src/common/decorators/pagination.decorator.ts` and internally applies `@ApiOkResponse`.
- Response DTOs belong in `<module>/dto/<entity>-response.dto.ts` and must be annotated with `@ApiProperty` / `@ApiPropertyOptional`.
- If an endpoint has no response DTO yet, use `@ApiResponse({ status, description })` and track creating the DTO as technical debt.
- If a documented contract changes, update the DTO, the endpoint, `docs/backend/API_DOCUMENTATION_GUIDE.md` when the pattern changes, and any frontend handoff under `docs/frontend/`.
